{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>At the sound of the shofar</b> — when he hears the shofar he says 'Aha!' from abundant joy, like 'Aha! Aha!' (האח האח), and it is a word said of joy when a person's desire comes to him. <b>At the sound of the shofar</b> (בדי שופר) is like <b>for naught</b> (בדי ריק), and it is close to the reason of 'no remnant' (אין די בער)." "<b>He scents battle</b> — as it sounds, for so it is." "<b>The shout of captains</b> — commanders make them hear, and the teru'ah from afar."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:19.578755867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}